=== 6. Doppler factor g: computed from the ray, asymmetric, physically bounded ===
  g = nu_obs / nu_emit. For a static observer k_s = (1,0,0,0), so
  g_receiver = e and g_source follows from u at the crossing.
  The camera frame is built exactly as the shader builds it, including the
  azimuth offset alpha of the ray plane. Omitting alpha moves every crossing
  by pi/2 in the table coordinate and finds the wrong crossings.
  r_cam 21.16 Rs, inclination 80 deg, shadow half-angle 6.88 deg (sin(psi) = b_crit*sqrt(1-Rs/r)/r = 0.119846)
  offset  -40 deg  b/b_crit   5.287  alpha 1.571  no shading crossing
  offset  -34 deg  b/b_crit   4.588  alpha 1.571  no shading crossing
